        <h3>Ejercicio 8: Función f(x) = ln(x) de tercer grado para aproximar ln(2)</h3>
        <p>Con x<sub>0</sub> = 1, x<sub>1</sub> = 1.5, x<sub>2</sub> = 2.5 y x<sub>3</sub> = 4: a) Calcular valores f(x<sub>i</sub>), b) Construir polinomio de tercer grado, c) Aproximar ln(2), d) Calcular e<sub>abs</sub> y e<sub>rel</sub>.</p>
        <p><strong>Solución:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>a) Valores en los nodos:</strong> f(1) = ln(1) = 0; f(1.5) = ln(1.5) ≈ 0.405465; f(2.5) = ln(2.5) ≈ 0.916291; f(4) = ln(4) ≈ 1.386294</li>
          <li><strong>b) Polinomios base evaluados en x = 2:</strong></li>
          <li>L<sub>0</sub>(2) = (2 - 1.5)(2 - 2.5)(2 - 4) / [(1 - 1.5)(1 - 2.5)(1 - 4)] = (0.5)(-0.5)(-2) / [(-0.5)(-1.5)(-3)] = 0.5 / -2.25 = -2/9 ≈ -0.222222</li>
          <li>L<sub>1</sub>(2) = (2 - 1)(2 - 2.5)(2 - 4) / [(1.5 - 1)(1.5 - 2.5)(1.5 - 4)] = (1)(-0.5)(-2) / [(0.5)(-1)(-2.5)] = 1 / 1.25 = 0.8</li>
          <li>L<sub>2</sub>(2) = (2 - 1)(2 - 1.5)(2 - 4) / [(2.5 - 1)(2.5 - 1.5)(2.5 - 4)] = (1)(0.5)(-2) / [(1.5)(1)(-1.5)] = -1 / -2.25 = 4/9 ≈ 0.444444</li>
          <li>L<sub>3</sub>(2) = (2 - 1)(2 - 1.5)(2 - 2.5) / [(4 - 1)(4 - 1.5)(4 - 2.5)] = (1)(0.5)(-0.5) / [(3)(2.5)(1.5)] = -0.25 / 11.25 = -1/45 ≈ -0.022222</li>
          <li><strong>c) Aproximación:</strong> P<sub>3</sub>(2) = 0(-2/9) + 0.405465(0.8) + 0.916291(4/9) + 1.386294(-1/45) = 0 + 0.324372 + 0.407240 - 0.030807 ≈ 0.700805</li>
          <li><strong>d) Errores (con ln(2) ≈ 0.693147):</strong> e<sub>abs</sub> = |0.693147 - 0.700805| = 0.007658; e<sub>rel</sub> = 0.007658 / 0.693147 ≈ 0.011048 (1.10%)</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Ejercicio 9: Función f(x) = e<sup>-x<sup>2</sup></sup> para aproximar f(0.6)</h3>
        <p>Con x<sub>0</sub> = 0, x<sub>1</sub> = 0.25, x<sub>2</sub> = 0.5 y x<sub>3</sub> = 1.0: a) Calcular valores de la función en cada nodo, b) Aproximar f(0.6), c) Calcular e<sub>abs</sub> y e<sub>rel</sub>.</p>
        <p><strong>Solución:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>a) Valores en cada nodo:</strong> f(0) = e<sup>0</sup> = 1; f(0.25) = e<sup>-0.0625</sup> ≈ 0.939413; f(0.5) = e<sup>-0.25</sup> ≈ 0.778801; f(1.0) = e<sup>-1</sup> ≈ 0.367879</li>
          <li><strong>b) Polinomios base en x = 0.6 y aproximación:</strong></li>
          <li>L<sub>0</sub>(0.6) = (0.6 - 0.25)(0.6 - 0.5)(0.6 - 1.0) / [(0 - 0.25)(0 - 0.5)(0 - 1.0)] = (0.35)(0.1)(-0.4) / (-0.125) = -0.014 / -0.125 = 0.112</li>
          <li>L<sub>1</sub>(0.6) = (0.6 - 0)(0.6 - 0.5)(0.6 - 1.0) / [(0.25 - 0)(0.25 - 0.5)(0.25 - 1.0)] = (0.6)(0.1)(-0.4) / (0.046875) = -0.024 / 0.046875 = -0.512</li>
          <li>L<sub>2</sub>(0.6) = (0.6 - 0)(0.6 - 0.25)(0.6 - 1.0) / [(0.5 - 0)(0.5 - 0.25)(0.5 - 1.0)] = (0.6)(0.35)(-0.4) / (-0.0625) = -0.084 / -0.0625 = 1.344</li>
          <li>L<sub>3</sub>(0.6) = (0.6 - 0)(0.6 - 0.25)(0.6 - 0.5) / [(1.0 - 0)(1.0 - 0.25)(1.0 - 0.5)] = (0.6)(0.35)(0.1) / (0.375) = 0.021 / 0.375 = 0.056</li>
          <li>P<sub>3</sub>(0.6) = 1(0.112) + 0.939413(-0.512) + 0.778801(1.344) + 0.367879(0.056) = 0.112 - 0.480979 + 1.046709 + 0.020601 ≈ 0.698331</li>
          <li><strong>c) Errores (con f(0.6) = e<sup>-0.36</sup> ≈ 0.697676):</strong> e<sub>abs</sub> = |0.697676 - 0.698331| = 0.000655; e<sub>rel</sub> = 0.000655 / 0.697676 ≈ 0.000939 (0.094%)</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Ventajas y limitaciones de Lagrange</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Ventaja:</strong> No requiere puntos equidistantes ni cálculo de derivadas o diferencias divididas.</li>
          <li><strong>Limitación:</strong> Agregar un nuevo punto obliga a recalcular todos los polinomios base L<sub>i</sub>(x), y usar grados muy altos puede producir oscilaciones bruscas (fenómeno de Runge).</li>
        </ul>
